==========================================================================
LEG 7b  INERT SITES -- three edits that must change NOTHING
==========================================================================
  These are not weak tests.  Each asserts a positive property of
  the 1996 routine that a later wave could break by accident, and
  each would then fail loudly:

    BREAK_SPILL       :4089's int*float product needs 35 bits, so
                      a binary64 spill there cannot lose anything
    BREAK_PARENTSEED  :4199's VALUE is dead -- phase F overwrites
                      p_ray[q] for every moon.  The DRAW is live.
    BREAK_ZORDER      :4094's VALUE is dead -- phase G overwrites
                      p_ring[n] for every planet.  The two draws
                      are live but the stream position is the same

  So 3 of the 17 float-site draws (:4094 x2, :4199 x1) feed values
  nothing in the routine ever reads.  14 are live.

  [PASS] BREAK_SPILL changes nothing, as claimed   0/55856 values differ
  [PASS] BREAK_SPILL leaves the draw ledger identical
  [PASS] BREAK_PARENTSEED changes nothing, as claimed   0/55856 values differ
  [PASS] BREAK_PARENTSEED leaves the draw ledger identical
